<title>USA: Kansas fed cattle Monday roundup - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas fed cattle Monday roundup - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with not</p>
<p>enough slaughter steers for a market test and no heifers</p>
<p>confirmed, USDA said. Inquiry was moderate and demand light.</p>
<p>Sales were confirmed on 100 slaughter steers and no</p>
<p>slaughter heifers confirmed. For week to date including late</p>
<p>Friday and the weekend on 4,200 formula and contract cattle.</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -</p>
<p>Pen mostly Select few Choice 2-3 1250 lbs 65.00.</p>
<p>Confirmed -    100   last week -  1,200   last year -    100</p>
<p>Wk to date - 4,200   last week - 17,200   last year - 33,300</p>
<p>Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
